AFAIR, the interface I mentioned upthread uses {40} for the weight
attribute; very simple, clear, and sufficient for the purpose. But
one can also implement w:{40} or w:40 if there's desire to keep the
syntax closer to the rest of the status line.

Mind that we have many more attributes without unit on the status
line; actually none[*] with a unit; St:9 Dx:18 Co:16 In:17 Wi:12 Ch:7
HP:68(68) Pw:63(129) AC:-3 Xp:10/5373, and even an attribute like
"turns"(that is unit-less in real life) or "time" (T:11431) has no
imaginable real-life equivalent to a complete turn (because of the
effect of speed intrinsic), or some specified time (because you play
turn-based).

Janis

